<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">expŏlītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		expolio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a smoothing off</i>, <i>rubbing
			up</i>, <i>polishing</i>, <i>finishing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">parietum, pavimentorum,</span>”
				<i>a plastering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6
						<i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7</span></i> praef. <i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbana,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of a house in the city</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Q. Fr. 3, 1, 2, § 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miniacea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
					9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of speech, <i>an
				adorning</i>, <i>embellishing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in verbis inest quasi materia quaedam: in
					numero autem expolitio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 55, 185</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 1, 12, 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Inv.
				1, 40, 74</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In partic., as a fig. of speech, <i><span class="en">Auct.
				Her. 4, 42, 54 sq.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
